    "00.kernel/00.00.10.work/0700.band.colabs/01.md"
  ],
  "instructions": [
    {
      "nn": "01",
      "heading": "Transport support only",
      "text": "This is the accepted assembler's draft, kept under support/ for custody checks. It is not an instruction source. Read ENTRY.md, then 05.01.pack.md."
    },
    {
      "nn": "02",
      "heading": "Method",
      "text": "Read the target contract as if you had to implement a consumer of it. Try to construct a sequence of files and events where a reader would believe a review or acceptance exists when it does not, or where two editable copies of a return could diverge. Say which sentence of the contract allows it, and what single rule would stop it."
    },
    {
      "nn": "03",
      "heading": "Case C01",
      "text": "A review template is copied into the investigation page before any return arrives. What tells a later reader it is not a review?"
    },
    {
      "nn": "04",
      "heading": "Case C02",
      "text": "A return arrives, is captured, and is then edited on the investigation page to fix a typo. Which record wins, and how would anyone notice?"
    },
    {
      "nn": "05",
      "heading": "Case C03",
      "text": "The Director replies informally in chat and nobody records it. What does 06.01.review.md show, and is that safe?"
    },
    {
      "nn": "06",
      "heading": "Return",
      "text": "Return one file shaped like templates/05.01.return.TEMPLATE.md. Prime places it as 05.01.return.md only after capture; this package does not contain it."
    }
  ],
  "evidence": "One return file in the return template shape. A receipt of it is custody, not acceptance.",
